# UST.G3CC Selected Source Terminal B89 Dualization

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_TERMINAL_B89_SELECTED_SOURCE_H02_VECTOR_AND_SPECTRAL_COVECTOR_HORIZONTAL_TRANSPORT_OPEN`

## Theorem

Take the exact G3CA source

```text
S_delta = u*v*P_delta*(t0*t1*t2)*C_section
```

and reduce the same 100-term characteristic-zero polynomial at the terminal
B89 good fiber `(11,gamma-3)`. Of its exact terms, 94 survive before quotient
reduction. Its ordinary-Jacobian normal form lies entirely in the frozen B103
H02 basis and emits a nonzero vector with

```text
229 / 248 nonzero H02 coordinates.
```

Independently multiply `S_delta` by every ordered B69 primitive H20 row and
reduce against the hash-locked B69 basis. Every one of the 248 products is a
scalar multiple of the promoted one-dimensional socle; there are zero bad
normal forms. The resulting spectral trace covector has

```text
227 / 248 nonzero entries.
```

Applying the inverse-transpose G3CB frame map produces the same covector in
the B103 H20-dual basis, with 224 nonzero entries. The exact identity

```text
spectral trace = M^T * B103 H20 dual
```

holds in all 248 coordinates. G3CB proves that the test rows are a basis, and
B72 perfect H20-H02 residue pairing therefore identifies these values as the
unique covector induced by the same selected H02 source class.

## Consequence

The selected normalized-delta correction source now has three mutually
consistent terminal good-fiber descriptions:

```text
B103 H02 class coordinates,
B69 spectral trace values,
B103 H20-dual values.
```

This closes the terminal source-value and row-frame obligations. A successor
transport calculation can consume the B103 source and emit its terminal
readout without either guessing a source vector or identifying unlike row
orders.

## Boundary

G3CC evaluates the local source term at the terminal fiber. It does not solve
the inhomogeneous rank-1,510 horizontal system, prove that this local source
section is horizontal, reconstruct characteristic-zero coordinate values,
produce the flat rank-1,509 or integral Betti lift, normalize a meridian, or
compute the normal function and `beta_C`.

